VI. Protection of User's Personal Information

6.1 It is a fundamental principle of Tencent to protect users" personal information. Tencent will take reasonable measures to protect such information. Except for the circumstances prescribed by laws and regulations, Tencent will not disclose users’ personal information to any third party without permission. Tencent adopts professionally encrypted storage and transmission methods for relevant information, to ensure the security of users’ personal information.

6.2 You need to provide some necessary information when registering an account or using the Services. For example, you need to fill in your mobile number so that Tencent can provide you with account registration service or user identification; the "People Nearby" feature needs your consent to use your geographic location information; and the mobile contacts matching feature requires your authorization for accessing your mobile contacts. If relevant laws and regulations or policies of the People’s Republic of China have special provisions, you need to provide real identity information. If the information you provide is incomplete, you will not be able to use the Services or you may be restricted during usage.

6.3 In general, you may browse and modify your information at any time. However, you may not be able to modify the initial registration information and other verification information provided at the time of registration for the purpose of security and identification (such as the Weixin account appeal service). If you have registered a new Weixin account using an existing Weixin account, Tencent will consider the initially registered mobile number of the new account is the same as that of the existing Weixin account.

6.4 Tencent will apply a variety of security technologies and procedures to establish a sound management system to protect your personal information and avoid any unauthorized access, use or disclosure.

6.5 Tencent will not disclose your personal information to any company, organization or individual without your consent, except as provided by laws and regulations.

6.6 Tencent attaches great importance to the protection of personal information of minors. If you are a minor under 18 years of age, you need to obtain a written consent from your parents or legal guardians before using Tencent's services.

6.7 You may read Weixin Privacy Protection Guidelines to learn more about what information Weixin collects or retains, how it is used, rights of you and how Weixin protect your personal information and privacy.

VII. Main Rights and Obligations
7.1 Account Usage Standards

7.1.1 Prior to using the Services, you need to register a Weixin account via a mobile number or an existing Weixin account. You can also link a QQ account and e-mail to the Weixin account after registration. If you wish to register via linking an email address, please use one that’s not linked to the Weixin Official Accounts Platform. Tencent has the right to specify the preconditions for registering a new Weixin account with an existing Weixin account and the maximum number of new accounts you can register with an existing Weixin account. For details, refer to the information provided on the product page.

Tencent is entitled to change the form of account registration and the linking method according to users' needs or product needs. During use of your account, please abide by the QQ ID Rules, Standards of Weixin Account Usage, related agreements for use of accounts, and special rules published by Tencent, regardless of how you register your Weixin account as agreed herein.

7.1.2 Ownership of all Weixin accounts belong to Tencent. After completing the application for registration, the user only obtains the right to use the Weixin account, and the usage right only belongs to the initial registrant. Meanwhile, the initial registrant shall not donate, borrow, rent, transfer or sell the Weixin account, or otherwise permit the non-initial applicant to use the Weixin account. Non-initial registrants shall not use Weixin account by donation, inheritance, lease, assignment or any other means.

7.1.3 The user is responsible for safekeeping the registration account information and password. The user shall assume legal responsibility for the registered account and password. The user agrees not to disclose the account and password information to others under any circumstance. When you suspect that someone else is using your account, you should immediately notify Tencent. If you register a new Weixin account through your existing Weixin account, Tencent may require you to use the above "Existing Weixin Account" for relevant auxiliary operations for the purpose of ensuring your account security, including but not limited to login verification, password recovery, account freezing, and appeal submissions, etc. If you have linked the new Weixin account with a different mobile phone number from the above-mentioned "Existing Weixin Account", the above-mentioned "Existing Weixin Account" will lose the ability to implement relevant auxiliary operations for the new Weixin account, and the action is irreversible. You should operate with caution.

7.1.4 When the user registers the Weixin account with a mobile phone number, the system will automatically generate a Weixin ID. You can set the Weixin ID, and it can be modified on the premise of meeting the corresponding conditions according to the guidance of relevant function pages.

7.1.5 When you use a service or feature of the software, you may be required to create or register a new account ("feature account") based on your Weixin account by following the instructions provided. Unless otherwise specified or authorized by Tencent in writing, such account shall be owned by Tencent, and the user who applies for, creates and registers the account ("initial registrant") only has the right to use the account. The initial registrant shall not give, borrow, lease, transfer, or sell such accounts to any other users or otherwise license such account for use by any other users. Any user other than the initial registrant shall not receive the account as a gift or transferred property, or purchase, inherit, lease, or any other means to use the account.

7.1.6 In the event of a user not logging in to a Weixin account or feature account for a prolonged period after registration or creation of such an account, Tencent has the right to recall the account to avoid waste of resources, and the user shall be solely responsible for all losses arising from such situations.

